<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		The abaddon's abdomen draws over her right wing (user's report, 2026-10-03: "the abdomen is
		displaying in front of the wing"), in the view she stands in by default - facing the camera.

		The numbers that matter are in two mods, and the wing side has a trap in it:

		  * VRE's cosmetic spawning sack is a render node under the Body tag. Its layer is written as
		    `drawData/defaultData/layer -3`, and only the north view carries a real per-facing layer
		    (90). South, east and west have an offset and no layer, and `defaultData` is not the
		    fallback - `PawnRenderNodeWorker.LayerFor` calls `DrawData.LayerForRot(facing,
		    Props.baseLayer)`. So the sack draws at `baseLayer`, which the def never sets: zero.
		  * Big & Small's winged tracker keeps four wing nodes in the s/e/w views. The right inner
		    wing has its `dataSouth` block commented out in their file (line 85 of
		    RaceTracker_WingedHuman.xml) and the right back wing has no south entry at all, so both
		    fall back to `baseLayer` zero as well. The left inner wing keeps a real -1.

		Zero against zero: the abdomen and those two wings are at the same depth, the sack is
		appended later, and it wins. That is the whole bug, and it is why the report names the right
		wing - the left one is at -1 and loses to the sack for an honest reason, while the right one
		is at the same level and loses a tie.

		Three operations, per node, and none of them touches the north view's own numbers:

		  * the inner wings get `baseLayer 1`, which is what the right one falls back to in every
		    view that has no entry of its own. The left one's south is explicit and is replaced to
		    match, so the pair stays symmetric.
		  * the back wings get `baseLayer 0.5`: above the sack, below the inner pair, and the order
		    between the wings is unchanged.
		  * the back wings also get a north layer of 90.5, because in the north view the sack's own
		    90 applies and the right back wing has no north override at all. 90.5 sits above the
		    sack and below the near wings' 91 and 92 there.

		Gated on Big and Small by display name: the xpath can only match that mod's tracker, and a
		patch operation that matches nothing is an error in the log.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
		<mods>
			<li>Big and Small - Framework</li>
		</mods>
		<match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
			<operations>
				<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
					<xpath>Defs/*[defName="BS_HumanoidWithWings_Race"]/renderNodeProperties/li[conditionalGraphics/conditionalPaths/altDefs/li="BS_FeatheredWingInner"]</xpath>
					<value>
						<baseLayer>1</baseLayer>
					</value>
				</li>
				<li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
					<xpath>Defs/*[defName="BS_HumanoidWithWings_Race"]/renderNodeProperties/li[conditionalGraphics/conditionalPaths/altDefs/li="BS_FeatheredWingInner"]/drawData/dataSouth/layer</xpath>
					<value>
						<layer>1</layer>
					</value>
				</li>
				<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
					<xpath>Defs/*[defName="BS_HumanoidWithWings_Race"]/renderNodeProperties/li[conditionalGraphics/conditionalPaths/altDefs/li="BS_FeatheredWingBack"]</xpath>
					<value>
						<baseLayer>0.5</baseLayer>
					</value>
				</li>
				<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
					<xpath>Defs/*[defName="BS_HumanoidWithWings_Race"]/renderNodeProperties/li[conditionalGraphics/conditionalPaths/altDefs/li="BS_FeatheredWingBack"]/drawData</xpath>
					<value>
						<dataNorth>
							<layer>90.5</layer>
						</dataNorth>
					</value>
				</li>
			</operations>
		</match>
	</Operation>
</Patch>
